  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Speaking with Duke Long, Fairy Zi Wei plans a Red Lotus true inheritance search and further time path Immortal Gu Houses, Three Autumn Yellow Crane Platform and Shark Flow Lever, so that four houses can block Fang Yuan in the River of Time.",
      "chapters": [
        1611
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_duke_long",
        "char_fairy_zi_wei",
        "inh_red_lotus_true_inheritance",
        "sys_immortal_gu_house",
        "house_three_autumn_yellow_crane_platform",
        "house_shark_flow_lever",
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "loc_river_of_time"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Deviation (recorded): this page is filed under gu-houses because Eternal Yacht is a named Immortal Gu House. It is mobile equipment of Heavenly Court, not a five-region map seat.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_heavenly_court"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "After Fang Yuan destroys Present and Past Pavilion in the River of Time, Eternal Yacht arrives too late, and the Gu Immortals aboard hesitate between saving the Four Xunzi and chasing him. Fang Yuan already treats Eternal Yacht as Heavenly Court’s other time path Immortal Gu House beside Present and Past Pavilion.",
      "chapters": [
        1629
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "river-arrival",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "house_present_and_past_pavilion",
        "sys_gu_immortal",
        "char_shang_xunzi"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Qing Ye, a Gu Immortal at rank eight, stands on Eternal Yacht with the Four Xunzi and others aboard. He later refuses pursuit and states that among three Immortal Gu Houses present, Eternal Yacht is the fastest but has the weakest defense, and that Fang Yuan’s time cutting edge pierces it.",
      "chapters": [
        1633
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "speed-and-defense",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_qing_ye"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "When Heavenly Court reaches the final step of constructing Eternal Yacht again, Cong Yan inserts rule path Immortal Gu Permanence into the incomplete house. The house shatters; Permanence survives because Cong Yan shields it as the core that cannot be harmed. Fairy Zi Wei then tells Duke Long that Eternal Yacht’s construction failed and must be redone, while Present and Past Pavilion remains in the River of Time.",
      "chapters": [
        1795
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "construction-failure",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_cong_yan",
        "sys_immortal_gu",
        "gu_permanence_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Eternal Yacht has the form of a multi-storied ship, larger than Myriad Year Flying Warship but not as fast. Fairy Zi Wei later judges Present and Past Pavilion and Eternal Yacht as only rank seven, yet outstanding among their peers. Fang Yuan’s Myriad Year Flying Warship smashes through Eternal Yacht until the house is destroyed and Qing Ye falls into the River of Time.",
      "chapters": [
        1806
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "form-and-destruction",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "house_myriad_year_flying_warship"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "In a later River of Time operation, Eternal Yacht is already waiting above a stone lotus island and is the first house to discover it. The Gu Immortals aboard quickly inform Heavenly Court, which sends the other Immortal Gu Houses to join.",
      "chapters": [
        1881
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "lotus-island-watch",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_heavenly_court"
      ]
    }
  ],
